      "title": "Troubleshooting Configuration Propagation Issues in Config Manager",
      "content_summary": "Addresses service unresponsiveness and data mismatches caused by configuration drift or propagation failures. Provides guidance on verifying environment variables and feature flags when changes do not take effect.",
      "content_body": "When users report service unresponsiveness or data mismatches, first check if the latest configuration has successfully propagated to all nodes. Configuration drift often occurs due to conflicting settings or operator errors during manual updates. Verify that required environment variables are present and that feature flags align with the intended state. If issues persist, review the access logs to identify recent policy misconfigurations or customer configuration errors. Typically, resolving these issues requires a configuration change or policy correction, followed by customer education on best practices for setting management. Note that older versions of Config Manager required a manual restart to apply global changes, unlike the current auto-refresh mechanism."
